The files in this directory come from three sources, each keeping its licence.

From the MAME project (https://github.com/mamedev/mame), BSD-3-Clause:

  z80.c, z80.h                src/devices/cpu/z80/z80.cpp, z80.h, z80.inc
                              Juergen Buchmueller; taken from pico-galagino,
                              which took it from pico-mooncresta
  z80.lst                     src/devices/cpu/z80/z80.lst, unchanged
                              Juergen Buchmueller, Andrei I. Holub
  z80_ops.h                   generated from z80.lst by tools/z80gen.py,
                              which is derived from src/devices/cpu/z80/
                              z80make.py: Andre I. Holub
  c1943.c, c1943_sound.c,     src/mame/capcom/1943.cpp, 1943_v.cpp
  c1943_video.c, c1943_gfx.c, (memory maps, interrupts, video hardware, layer
  c1943_sets.c                priorities, colour PROMs, graphics layouts, ROM
                              sets): Paul Leaman. The table of the i8751's
                              answers is MAME 0.185's c1943_protection_r.

From ymfm (https://github.com/aaronsgiles/ymfm), BSD-3-Clause:

  ym_ssg.c, ym_ssg.h          src/ymfm_ssg.cpp (ssg_engine): Aaron Giles

From the MAME project, GPL-2.0-or-later (here under the GPL v3.0, as the
rest of the project):

  ym2203.c, ym2203.h          src/devices/sound/fm.cpp of MAME 0.229, the
                              YM2203 path: Jarek Burczynski, Tatsuyuki Satoh,
                              with fixes by Eke-Eke (Genesis Plus GX)

romload.c (from pico-galagino's, itself from pico-mooncresta's), c1943.h,
c1943_internal.h, c1943_port.h, c1943_input.c/.h and c1943_store.c/.h are
original to the family of emulators and are distributed with the rest of the
project under the GNU General Public License v3.0. The parts of c1943_video.c
that place the picture in the canvas follow pico-galagino's gal_core.c (GPL
v3.0).

